<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Ha Dong by Motorbike: Motorbike Rental Planning in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Ha Dong is the city&rsquo;s southwestern corner, the district that was a town of its own before the city grew out to meet it, and a rider based here plans a rental with an honest map, wide corridors that carry real flow, an old-town layer of local streets around the market blocks, and a centre trip that is the longest of the southwestern bases. The rental counter is not in the neighbourhood, it is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, reached by crossing the city&rsquo;s middle and then the water on the bridges toward the Hoan Kiem side. This page plans the rental honestly from a Ha Dong base, the pickup project, the machine choice, the period arithmetic and the first week, with no invented journey times, no branches that do not exist and no promises the desk has not made.</p>
<p>We cover where Ha Dong sits in the riding map, the pickup project and its crossing, the district&rsquo;s daily riding pattern, what the handover includes, choosing machine and period with verified prices, the questions worth asking the desk, parking and security habits, and the first week in order. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and the verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, check the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost</a> page for the full price picture, and browse wider riding advice in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>.</p>
